# Gromit configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the repository root (right next to this file) and
# fill in the value. `src/gromit/cli.py` calls python-dotenv's `load_dotenv()`
# at import, and that search starts at the directory the `gromit` package was
# imported from and walks upward — so with the editable install the README
# describes (`uv pip install -e .`), a `.env` in this checkout is found no
# matter which directory you run `gromit` from, while a `.env` sitting in some
# unrelated working directory is NOT read. If you are unsure, or installed
# non-editably, just export HF_TOKEN in your shell: an exported variable is
# always read and always wins over `.env`.
#
# HF_TOKEN below is the ONLY variable Gromit reads. Everything else is a
# command-line flag — model size, language, device and verbosity are
# `--model`, `--language`, `--device` and `--verbose`; see `gromit --help`.

# HuggingFace token, used only by `gromit transcribe` for pyannote's gated
# speaker-diarization models. Read-only permissions are enough.
#   1. Accept the licence at
#      https://huggingface.co/pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1
#   2. Create a token at https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
HF_TOKEN=
